    Bug 1923153 - Improve imap keyswap handling. r=mkmelin,leftmostcat

    This was found while moving a single IMAP message, which gets a fake
    messageKey in the new folder and later triggers the `msgKeyChanged`
    event: fakeMessageKey -> serverMessageKey.

    There will be no secondary swap for serverMessageKey -> fakeMessageKey.
    These mirror swaps only occur, if the code almost guessed the correct
    messageKeys while moving multiple messages, and the keys assigned
    by the server are swapped.

    The patch will register a pending mirror event only if it is really
    expected. This also removes the no longer valid entry from the
    MessageTracker.

    We perform a similar action when attachments are removed from messages.
    The core message database is handling the modified message without
    attachments as a new message with a new messageKey. The WebExtension API
    does not, but updates the tracker information with the new messageKey.
    The old tracker information was also not removed and could cause issues.
    This might be the reason for Bug 1910483.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D224927

